    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0093" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/549</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Egan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-11T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 12, 2.10 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>568. At a conference to-day at Copenhagen between German and Russian Socialists,
                    the German Socialists stated that they would endeavor to move the German
                    Reichstag to consent to peace on the following terms, provided the Russian
                    Socialists would make a similar effort in Russia.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Germany shall evacuate the occupied territories in northern France and
                        Belgium, which latter country shall be reestablished as an independent state
                        but without the right to maintain an army. Alsace-Lorraine shall remain
                        German. Poland to be reestablished on the basis of its original boundaries:
                        excepted however are the Polish provinces which were held by Germany before
                        the war. Poland shall have no right to maintain an army. The Russian Baltic
                        provinces shall be surrendered to Germany. Bulgaria,<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d26-f1"/> Servia, and Montenegro to be united in one kingdom
                        called Great Servia under Austrian protection. The Dardanelles to be
                        neutralized and under Turkish supervision. Armenia shall be reestablished
                        also under Turkish supervision.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d26-f1" n="1" xml:id="d26-f1-content">
                <p>On Apr. 12, in his telegram No. 573, the Minister added: “Read Bosnia and
                    Herzegovina instead of Bulgaria. In addition Roumania was to be reestablished.”
                    (File No. 763.72119/551.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
